{
  "title": "An EVA-only bounded escape round-trips but misses the observed public escape syntax",
  "program": "L3",
  "on_path": true,
  "hard": true,
  "statement": "A prefix-reserved, exactly reversible escape using only EVA a/e/i/o/y glyphs handles unknown lowercase ASCII words of length at most 16; longer words are explicitly refused. Across four historical books and three random codebook assignments, with 5,000 assigned entries, 2,166\u20136,452 of 25,000 planted test words use the escape and 0\u20134 are refused. The escaped tokens average 28.55\u201330.98 EVA glyphs, and a simple fixed-width charge for their five-symbol stream is 201,294\u2013557,400 bits; the compressed dictionary alone costs 224,168\u2013245,536 bits. None of the 5,461 ZL or 5,394 IT public practice-evaluation tokens is a valid escaped word under this frozen syntax. The channel therefore provides no literal escape coverage of those samples, despite exact planted round-trips; dictionary membership is not decipherment.",
  "check": "Before any hidden-page test, design a documented historical or otherwise well-motivated bounded escape whose valid encoded forms occur in an independently chosen public training set and are distinguishable from dictionary words. Include complete codec and dictionary charges, a normalized model for transmitted ciphertext, plaintext and preimage costs, explicit treatment of refused words, and unknown-key recovery calibrated on disjoint planted data. Compare fixed dictionary-only, escape-only and combined variants without changing the syntax on the final evaluation. Do not count an arbitrary dictionary hit as a reading.",
  "method": "Use public training ZL paragraph words for the candidate codebook after excluding all y-initial words (5,797 types), and reserve y as escape prefix. For each lowercase ASCII byte emit four base-four digits a/e/i/o, preceded once by y; decode validates each byte, length 1\u201316, and exact syntax. Encode whole words, preserving spaces; reject rather than silently alter any longer OOV word. Fit plaintext frequency ranks on the first 50,000 tokens of each hash-verified historical reference; assign 1,000 or 5,000 random codewords with seeds 17/37/73; encode and exactly decode the next 25,000 tokens. Evaluate dictionary membership and strict escape syntax on the public ZL/IT practice-evaluation witnesses. Count dictionary JSON compressed by the project\u2019s judge, compressed codec-function source separately, 3 bits per five-symbol escape glyph as a fixed-width cost, and literal UTF-8 plaintext size as an accounting reference. These component sizes are not a full MDL score and must not be summed without specifying the whole coding scheme.",
