  "limitations": "This deliberately simple escaped spelling is a diagnostic construction, not a historically sourced cipher or a claim that the selected marker was used in the manuscript. A valid escape is not automatically a sensible plaintext, and no key is inferred. Dictionary assignments are random and use public Voynich training types, so membership is not recovery; reference windows and generated texts are not independent of their own fitted training vocabulary. ZL and IT transcribe the same pages. The 16-character cap refuses some test words; none is silently accepted. Fixed-width and compressed JSON costs are descriptive components, omit full program, plaintext distribution and preimage charges, and do not constitute the judge\u2019s full model score. No secret held-out manuscript pages were accessed."
